Samsung Exynos7570: Samsung Galaxy J4 (SM-J400F)
================================================

Kernel: 6.12 with the J4 port (github.com/manoedinata/linux, branch
exynos7570-6.12) as patches-6.12/. Mobile data needs the "j4" feed
(feeds.conf.default): samsungipcd and ModemManager with its plugin.

Build:

  ./scripts/feeds update -a
  ./scripts/feeds install -a
  ./scripts/feeds install -p j4 -f -a   # this modemmanager replaces the stock one
  cp j4lte.diffconfig .config
  make defconfig
  make

CONFIG_KERNEL_DEVTMPFS and CONFIG_KERNEL_DEVMEM (in j4lte.diffconfig) are
required: they override the target's kernel config, and the boot ramdisk
mounts devtmpfs and writes the boot reason through /dev/mem.

Install: S-BOOT only boots an Android boot image, so the kernel Image and
exynos7570-j4lte.dtb are wrapped by uniLoader with mainline-tools/pack.sh
from github.com/Manoedinata/debian_j4lte (root=/dev/mmcblk0p25) and written
to BOOT (mmcblk0p10). The rootfs tarball goes onto USERDATA (mmcblk0p25),
formatted ext4. If that is done from the stock 3.18 kernel, format with
"mkfs.ext4 -O ^metadata_csum": 3.18 corrupts the superblock checksum of a
metadata_csum filesystem.

The only network link is the USB RNDIS gadget (rndis0 in br-lan,
172.16.42.1); mobile data comes up as the wwan interface on rmnet0.
